Report
This practical covered Oracle 21c pluggable database (PDB) administration.
I created a new PDB with a dedicated user, verified it through SHOW PDBS and DBA_USERS, 
then practiced the full lifecycle by creating and dropping a temporary PDB. 
I also configured Oracle Enterprise Manager Express on port 5500,
confirming it was listening via netstat and reachable via a curl request that returned HTTP 200. 
Together these steps demonstrate core SQL*Plus skills: multitenant database creation, user management, safe PDB removal,
and verifying Oracle's web-based administration console was correctly set up and running.
